  "caption_latex": "\\textbf{Local coupling, remote correlations.} Each spin couples to its own cavity, with photon hopping between cavities and no direct spin interaction. {The numerical plots show neighbouring concurrence in (a), endpoint concurrence in (b), real endpoint photon coherence in (c), and connected photon-number covariance in (d).} Uniform number losses $(0.2,0.2,0.2)\\omega_c$ and weak ends $(0.04,0.52,0.04)\\omega_c$ have the same total loss. The hopping curves use $J_b=0.25\\omega_c$; the $J_b=0$ cross correlations vanish by factorisation. Spins start in $\\ket{ggg}$ and cavities in vacuum, with $\\omega_s=0.1\\omega_c$, $g_+/g_-=1/4$ and $g_-^2+g_+^2=0.18\\,\\omega_c^2$. Solid curves and pointwise 95\\% bands are nonlinear HOPS; same-colour dotted curves are photon-cutoff-checked master equations. There is no measurement or feedback. Schematic artwork generated with AI."
